From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elena Maher <12779416+elenaOnline@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 22:26:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] gpui: Add Window::with_font_smoothing

On macOS, glyphs are rasterized with Core Graphics' font smoothing, which
dilates strokes (by a color-dependent amount for light text). Web content
styled with -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased renders the plain outline
coverage instead, and there was no way to match it.

FontSmoothing { PlatformDefault, Antialiased } is part of RenderGlyphParams
(so both rasterizations can share the atlas), and
Window::with_font_smoothing scopes it like with_element_opacity. With
Antialiased, the macOS rasterizer turns smoothing off and uses no dilation,
and subpixel rendering is skipped. The default is unchanged; platforms
without font smoothing draw both alike.
---
 crates/gpui/src/platform.rs             | 13 +++++++
 crates/gpui/src/text_system.rs          |  6 ++--
 crates/gpui/src/window.rs               | 46 ++++++++++++++++++++-----
 crates/gpui_macos/src/text_system.rs    |  8 +++--
 crates/gpui_windows/src/direct_write.rs |  1 +
 5 files changed, 61 insertions(+), 13 deletions(-)

diff --git a/crates/gpui/src/platform.rs b/crates/gpui/src/platform.rs
index c03653e..5141668 100644
--- a/crates/gpui/src/platform.rs
+++ b/crates/gpui/src/platform.rs
@@ -2480,6 +2480,19 @@ pub enum TextRenderingMode {
     Grayscale,
 }
 
+/// How glyph edges are rasterized, like CSS `-webkit-font-smoothing`.
+#[derive(Copy, Clone, Debug, Default, PartialEq, Eq, Hash)]
+pub enum FontSmoothing {
+    /// The platform's font smoothing, as native text gets (CSS `auto`). On macOS this thickens
+    /// glyph strokes, more for light text on dark backgrounds.
+    #[default]
+    PlatformDefault,
+    /// Grayscale anti-aliasing of the plain glyph outline, without smoothing (CSS
+    /// `antialiased`): lighter strokes, the same for every color. Platforms without font
+    /// smoothing draw both alike.
+    Antialiased,
+}
+
 /// The options that can be configured for a file dialog prompt
 #[derive(Clone, Debug)]
 pub struct PathPromptOptions {
